content:
The cuboid is \(3\times2\times2\), so it contains \(12\) cubes.

1. From the visible front face, the colours are:

\[
\begin{array}{ccc}
\text{light} & \text{dark} & \text{dark}\\
\text{light} & \text{light} & \text{dark}
\end{array}
\]

2. Looking at the back layer, the upper row is:

\[
\begin{array}{ccc}
\text{light} & \text{white} & \text{dark}
\end{array}
\]

The lower-right cube is also white, as shown by the red outline on the side.

3. The light and dark pieces now each have four cubes, so the two hidden lower cubes in the back layer must be white. Thus the back layer is:

\[
\begin{array}{ccc}
\text{light} & \text{white} & \text{dark}\\
\text{white} & \text{white} & \text{white}
\end{array}
\]

The white piece therefore consists of three cubes in a row with one cube above the middle—a T-shape, matching option D.

\[
\boxed{\text{D}}
\]
